  "step_1": "The decision reason can be applied to the decision problem. The problem contains a sure outcome (Lottery B: -3000 Euros with 100% probability), so the reference value is -3000 Euros. The differences between each outcome and this reference value must be calculated and weighted by their probabilities. For Lottery A: outcome -4000 (80%) has a difference of (-4000) - (-3000) = -1000; outcome 0 (20%) has a difference of 0 - (-3000) = +3000. The mean difference for A is (0.8 × -1000) + (0.2 × 3000) = -800 + 600 = -200. For Lottery B: the only outcome is -3000, so the difference is 0 with 100% probability, and the mean difference is 0. The decision reason prefers the lottery with the more favorable (i.e., less negative or more positive) mean difference. Since 0 > -200, the reason would prefer Lottery B. Thus, the reason is applicable and leads to a preference for B.",
